m-Settings"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit defines a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/URL\/systemSettings","isActive":true},{"text":" URL that can be used to open your app in System Settings. This can be used to help users enable the keyboard, enable Full Access, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Tip","style":"tip","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your keyboard navigates to the System Settings root instead of your app, try adding an empty settings bundle to your app target."}]}]},{"text":"Opening the Main App from a Keyboard Extension","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Opening-the-Main-App-from-a-Keyboard-Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The best way to open the main app from its keyboard extension, is to trigger the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/openMainApp(_:withReason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" action to let the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/actionHandler","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" open the app. You can provide an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to tell the app why it was opened."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In the main app, you can then use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReason"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReasonCase"},{"text":" to see why it was opened, and show contextual information if needed. The open reason will automatically reset when the main app is sent to the background.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"tip","type":"aside","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit will automatically open your main app with the open reason ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when starting dictation, then try to navigate back to the keyboard once dictation has been started."}]}]},{"anchor":"Returning-to-the-Keyboard-Extension-from-the-Main-App","type":"heading","text":"Returning to the Keyboard Extension from the Main App","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext","isActive":true},{"text":" has a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext\/hostApplicationBundleId","isActive":true},{"text":" (see the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" article for more information) that can be mapped to a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", you can trigger the app’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication\/open(withAction:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to return to the keyboard.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"However, since KeyboardKit only knows about the most common apps, you can’t rely on this. 